Error [E0622]: A module binding's value must be a literal
  --> tests/ui/module_value_call.jet:9:9
    |
  9 | GRAY :: gray(U8{128})
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A module constant is folded once while building, so its value must be literal data: numbers, text, typed literals, and enum cases
 Fix: Write the value as literal data, such as `Rgb{r: U8{0}, g: U8{0}, b: U8{0}}`, or compute it inside a function
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0622

Error [E0622]: A module binding's value must be a literal
  --> tests/ui/module_value_call.jet:10:11
    |
 10 | CURSOR := Rgb{r: U8{255}, g: U8{255}, b: U8{255}}
    |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A mutable or `#Persist` module global is runtime storage, which every execution tier initializes from a scalar literal before `fn run`
 Fix: Use an integer, float, or bool literal, or keep struct and list values in an unmarked `::` constant
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0622
